### Asynch Upgrade - but not a true test in sqlite locally - ensure you test once deployed to SAP BTP
### Stop the service, add a new number range in package.json, restart the serivice and run this command
### Expect existing number ranges to be untouched (ie maintain current values) and new number ranges to be created with initial value
# @name asynchJob
POST http://localhost:4004/-/cds/saas-provisioning/upgrade
content-type: application/json
Authorization: Basic yves:
Prefer: respond-async

{ "tenants": ["*"] }

### Unsubscribe tenant t1
POST http://localhost:4004/-/cds/deployment/unsubscribe
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Basic yves:

{
  "tenant": "t1"
}

### Unsubscribe tenant t2
POST http://localhost:4004/-/cds/deployment/unsubscribe
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Basic yves:

{
  "tenant": "t2"
}